From b67cd8cf1520e86c5441c522e9bbee9badabfd95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:05:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): expire non-claiming metrics and scope lease
 refusals [daveey]

A stale claiming=0 metric survived indefinitely in portable placement. Match the
Board fresh window (90 seconds, milliseconds) with coordination future skew;
thread one optional now through both consumers. Preserve machine pins and bare
pickup semantics. Unknown/malformed timestamps do not veto placement.

Treat Board not_claiming grants as recorder-only refusals and retain their
placement capacity evidence, not a fleet-wide verdict.

Reason-consumer audit:
- kanban_dispatch_skip._RECORDER_ONLY: add; the recorder cannot lease it.
- kanban_capacity_evidence._task_reasons: add to per-machine placement evidence.
- kanban_db_dispatch.DispatchResult: examples in documentation, no exhaustive
  validator; arbitrary Board claim refusal strings are already retained.
- kanban_dispatch_expected_holds: do not add. Its foreign set denotes excluded
  label rows, not transient self-claim shutdown; preserve stuck accounting for
  an unexplained non-claiming dispatcher, rather than calling it an expected hold.
- kanban_worker_node.eligible: do not add. This is a preflight of durable labels,
  pins and holds. The Board owns grant-time claiming freshness; consulting this
  machine's own cached claiming bit could perpetuate the hold after recovery.
- kanban_db_dispatch_preclaim: labels_mismatch alone emits a fleet-unplaceable
  diagnostic; not_claiming proves no missing labels and must not emit it.
- kanban_diagnostics and kanban_label_backlog: explanatory label mismatch text,
  no refusal allowlists; no change.
- remaining pinned_only hits in sync routes, sessions_cmd and state maintenance
  describe registry/session fields, not Board refusal enumerations.

Tests first: freshness suite failed 24 cases on base, then passed; skip suite
failed all 3 new cases before implementation. Existing giveup fixture metrics
now carry fresh at values; assertions and pin/bare pickup behavior unchanged.
